## Managed by Ansible (roles/hardening) — local edits are overwritten.
##
## Numbered 10 so it is read BEFORE the cloud image's 60-cloudimg-settings.conf. sshd takes the
## FIRST value it obtains for a keyword and Include sits at the top of sshd_config, so inside
## sshd_config.d a LOWER number wins. That is the opposite of most drop-in directories, and it is
## the reason a 99- file here would lose to anything the image ships.

## Keys only.
##
## The cloud image ships this exact setting as `#PasswordAuthentication no` — commented out — so
## the effective value was sshd's built-in default of `yes`. No account on this host has a
## password, so nothing could actually have authenticated that way, but it was one `passwd` away
## from being untrue on a host with port 22 open to the internet.
PasswordAuthentication no
KbdInteractiveAuthentication no
PermitEmptyPasswords no
PubkeyAuthentication yes

## Stricter than the three above together: nothing but a public key is even offered, regardless of
## what PAM would otherwise be willing to try.
AuthenticationMethods publickey

PermitRootLogin no

## Membership is the grant. Adding a Unix account no longer implies SSH access, which is what makes
## the executor's future service account safe to create.
AllowGroups {{ hardening_ssh_group }}

MaxAuthTries {{ hardening_ssh_max_auth_tries }}
LoginGraceTime {{ hardening_ssh_login_grace_time }}

## Logs the fingerprint of the key that authenticated. That is what makes "who deployed that"
## answerable after the fact, and it is what fail2ban counts.
LogLevel VERBOSE

X11Forwarding no

{% if hardening_ssh_allow_tcp_forwarding %}
## On enabled here because services on this host bind 127.0.0.1, which makes an SSH tunnel the
## intended way to reach them from a laptop. Where that is true it grants an authenticated user
## nothing they could not already do by running a command on the host; where the database lives on
## another machine it is a way to reach that machine, which is a different proposition.
AllowTcpForwarding yes
{% else %}
AllowTcpForwarding no
{% endif %}

## Drop sessions whose network has gone away rather than holding them open.
ClientAliveInterval 300
ClientAliveCountMax 2
